@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# Generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh; summaryText/decisionPoint
# hand-written per docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps
# are real (from `git log origin/main..HEAD` on branch
# issue-537-explain-endpoint, corrected from the script's first run because
# the worktree's local `main` ref was stale relative to origin/main).

ghpull:570 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "sparql_endpoint: EXPLAIN/profiling endpoint for query plans" ;
    bl:number 570 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:537 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr570 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:537 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-21T09:32:25Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-21T22:10:40Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr570Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #537 asked for an EXPLAIN/query-profiling endpoint (split out of #533's performance report) but left the design open: trigger mechanism, report contents, and format were all undecided. The plan doc was written before any code, per this repo's TDD workflow: read sparql_parser/src/join_ordering.rs and sparql_endpoint/src/query.rs first to find what already existed to reuse, rather than inventing new plan-computation logic. order_patterns already computes the exact BGP evaluation order eval_bgp uses; known_cardinality already computes the exact index-lookup cost. The EXPLAIN report calls these directly instead of re-deriving them. An advisor review after the first plan draft caught a real gap: the draft only mirrored join_ordering's BGP-internal ordering, missing that eval_components_budgeted also performs a purely static component-level reordering (component_ordering::should_reorder/order_components, Phase C of the join-reordering epic, #173) that hoists a constraining conjunct ahead of a UNION/OPTIONAL/MINUS it shares variables with -- and that per PR #173's own provenance summary, #533's actual reported pathology was exactly this component-level case, not a BGP-internal one. Fixing this before writing tests meant the multi-pattern test set needed a fourth case (UNION-hoist, mirroring component_ordering.rs's own moves_constraining_bgp_before_union fixture) to actually exercise that code path -- the first three tests never triggered should_reorder's len>=2-plus-Union/Optional/Minus gate. The advisor also flagged a duplicated-match risk (a second copy of known_cardinality's index-selection logic for the indexUsed field) that was resolved by refactoring known_cardinality into a thin wrapper around a new cardinality_and_index returning both the count and an IndexUsed enum, so the real join planner and EXPLAIN read from one source of truth. Trigger mechanism: ?explain=true on the existing GET/POST /sparql routes (which funnel through one run_select_query shared by /sparql and the per-dataset routes), returning JSON directly and bypassing SPARQL Results content negotiation entirely rather than inventing a fourth negotiated format or a separate /explain route that would duplicate query-string/body parsing. Timing is total wall-clock only (one Instant pair around the existing execute_with_base call), a deliberate scope cut from per-operator timing to keep the non-explain hot path completely untouched -- no new parameter or branch in eval_bgp/eval_component/eval_components_budgeted's signatures. Two edge cases surfaced only while wiring the HTTP layer, not during planning: run_transactional_query (txId reads) doesn't share run_select_query's explain handling, so explain+txId returns 400 rather than silently ignoring the parameter; and a first draft of the UNION test used a stray '.' directly after a UNION group's closing brace, which the parser rejects -- a syntax bug in the test fixture, not the explain logic, caught by running it and reading the actual parse-error response before assuming the component-reordering mirroring was wrong." ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr570Decision ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:570 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr570 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr570Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Mirror both sparql_parser::join_ordering's BGP-internal pattern order AND sparql_parser::component_ordering's component-level reordering (UNION/OPTIONAL/MINUS hoisting) in the static EXPLAIN walk, using the same empty already_bound/guaranteed_bound sets those functions receive at a query's top level and at every independently-evaluated scope (UNION arms, bare Group bodies, MINUS's RHS) -- exact, not approximate, in those cases." ;
    agp:alternative "An earlier draft mirrored only join_ordering (BGP pattern order) and let component_ordering's UNION/OPTIONAL/MINUS hoisting fall through as plain source order. Rejected after an advisor review pointed out that PR #173's own provenance summary identifies #533's actual reported pathology as exactly a component-level UNION-before-constraint case, not a BGP-internal cardinality-ordering case -- so a report that silently prints source order at the component level would misrepresent the one failure mode this endpoint was created to diagnose." .
